azgor schrieb:
> 
> This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
> freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.
> 
> [1]: An emergency way to blind yourself might be to stab your eyes out,
> like Oedipus.

Since that'd be permanent, i think it'd be utterly pointless outside
of challenge games (unwinnable, since you wouldn't be able to read the
Book of the Dead). Do they grow back when you ascend?

> [2]: Tinned fruit. That's all we really need now, isn't it? Tinned
> fruit, mate. --TheShrewdDude

Yes!
And different sorts, too!

> [4]: Snakes should hiss when you #chat with them. --BenUrban

If they don't already, they should.

> [5]: Optional handicaps: the ability to start the game hungry or with
> eroded armor, for instance. --azgor

These two wouldn't be particularly meaningful. Just taking off your
original armour and waiting on the stairs till hungry would achieve
the exact same.

> [6]: Humanoid and demonic characters have the ability to sexually abuse
> you.

Yuck. I don't want that in a game, thanks a lot.

> [7]: When hallucinating and hungry/weak from hunger, enemies should
> start appearing as %s, moreso when weak.

Or reserve food-related hallucinated monster names for characters who
got the munchies.

> [9]: The lurker above digests you! You finish engraving. <-- There
> should be some way to remedy this situation (being engulfed while
> engraving). --BenUrban

That's a bug report, not a new idea.

> [11]: Stacking to avoid a surcharge should exercise wisdom. --BenUrban

Possibly; but do we need even more ways to exercise wisdom?

> [13]: rocks fired from slings have a bonus against giants (David vs
> Goliath anyone?) --teabing

A +2 to-hit or +1 damage, why not?

> [15]: You should always have the option of same-sex-sex.

I think that'd be an option for a variant patch - allow to specify
sexual preference at game start. Don't know how to handle bisexuals: i
think it's a deliberate design decision that only about half the
*cubus population will try to make a pass on a character.

> [16]: A cursed container (besides a bag of holding) should have a
> chance of cursing its contents every time it is used. --TheShrewdDude

Not by using; but i think getting items in a container wet might
affect their b/u/c status - water which gets into a cursed
sack/oilskin sack turns into cursed water and thus curses items it
rusts, dilutes or blanks. Vice versa for blessed sacks of course.

